WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.418
And the stomach acid dissolves
everything like a cartoon vat?

00:00:04.169 --> 00:00:04.540
No.

00:00:04.950 --> 00:00:08.381
Hydrochloric acid helps kill
many microbes and provides acidic

00:00:08.383 --> 00:00:10.110
conditions for stomach protease.

00:00:10.619 --> 00:00:14.315
Enzymes work best within particular
temperature and pH ranges.

00:00:14.794 --> 00:00:18.575
Extreme conditions can change
their shape, called denaturing.

00:00:18.876 --> 00:00:21.144
They do not die because
they were never alive.

00:00:21.961 --> 00:00:24.828
Then bile is the enzyme that digests fat.

00:00:25.179 --> 00:00:27.010
I can hear the dramatic music already.

00:00:27.794 --> 00:00:29.406
Bile is not an enzyme.

00:00:29.653 --> 00:00:31.033
It emulsifies fat.

00:00:31.307 --> 00:00:34.016
Large globules become
many smaller droplets.

00:00:34.298 --> 00:00:38.624
That increases surface area for lipase,
which performs chemical digestion.

00:00:39.032 --> 00:00:41.875
Emulsification and digestion
are different jobs.

00:00:42.571 --> 00:00:45.078
Who makes bile, and where is it stored?

00:00:45.858 --> 00:00:48.396
The liver makes it, and
the gallbladder stores it.

00:00:48.784 --> 00:00:51.039
It is released into the small intestine.

00:00:51.514 --> 00:00:55.784
Alkaline bile helps neutralize
incoming acid alongside pancreatic

00:00:55.786 --> 00:00:59.694
secretions, providing conditions
suitable for intestinal enzymes.

00:01:00.462 --> 00:01:03.261
The accessory organs send
substances into the canal.

00:01:03.585 --> 00:01:05.736
Food itself does not enter those organs.

00:01:06.117 --> 00:01:07.715
Bile prepares the droplets.

00:01:07.941 --> 00:01:09.609
Lipase cuts the molecules

00:01:09.966 --> 00:01:12.864
Our food molecules are now
small enough to be absorbed.

00:01:13.481 --> 00:01:15.920
Does absorption mean the
same thing as digestion?

00:01:16.734 --> 00:01:17.045
No.

00:01:17.459 --> 00:01:19.428
Digestion breaks molecules down.

00:01:19.861 --> 00:01:23.216
Absorption moves the digested
products across the gut wall into

00:01:23.216 --> 00:01:24.773
the body's transport systems.

00:01:25.667 --> 00:01:26.513
Exactly.

00:01:26.918 --> 00:01:29.884
Most nutrient absorption
happens in the small intestine.

00:01:30.229 --> 00:01:34.063
Look at the folded lining and these
finger-like projections called villi.

00:01:34.526 --> 00:01:35.956
One is a villus.

00:01:36.763 --> 00:01:38.281
Large surface area again?

00:01:38.800 --> 00:01:42.823
Just like alveoli, but this time
the job is absorbing nutrients.

00:01:43.643 --> 00:01:44.168
Yes.

00:01:44.789 --> 00:01:48.780
Each villus has a thin surface layer,
so there is a short distance to cross.

00:01:49.215 --> 00:01:52.075
Blood capillaries carry
away sugars and amino acids.

00:01:52.415 --> 00:01:57.115
A central lymph vessel called a lacteal
transports much of the absorbed fat.

00:01:57.781 --> 00:02:01.071
So all absorbed fat goes straight
into the blood capillary?

00:02:01.816 --> 00:02:04.207
Much of it first enters the
lymphatic system through

00:02:04.208 --> 00:02:06.411
lacteals, then reaches the blood.

00:02:06.748 --> 00:02:10.343
We do not need the full chemistry
today, but we should not draw every

00:02:10.343 --> 00:02:12.619
nutrient taking exactly the same route.

00:02:13.420 --> 00:02:15.841
And everything crosses by diffusion?

00:02:16.634 --> 00:02:20.795
Some movement follows concentration
gradients, but absorption also uses

00:02:20.796 --> 00:02:22.754
specialized transport processes.

00:02:23.527 --> 00:02:27.207
Certain nutrients can be taken up
using energy-dependent transport.

00:02:27.559 --> 00:02:32.253
Thin walls and a large area help, but
absorption is not only simple diffusion.

00:02:33.045 --> 00:02:37.660
Once glucose reaches a cell, it can be
used in respiration to release energy.

00:02:38.444 --> 00:02:41.799
Amino acids can become new
proteins for growth and repair.

00:02:42.604 --> 00:02:46.431
That use of absorbed nutrients
by cells is called assimilation.

00:02:46.945 --> 00:02:51.049
Now, water is absorbed in both
the small and large intestines.

00:02:51.412 --> 00:02:54.222
The small intestine
absorbs most water overall.

00:02:54.522 --> 00:02:57.462
The large intestine recovers
water from what remains.

00:02:58.308 --> 00:03:01.780
So I should not write that only
the large intestine absorbs water.

00:03:02.231 --> 00:03:04.134
It finishes part of the recovery job.

00:03:04.866 --> 00:03:05.270
Good.

00:03:05.618 --> 00:03:09.647
Undigested material moves towards
the rectum, which stores feces

00:03:09.647 --> 00:03:11.191
until they leave through the anus.

00:03:11.503 --> 00:03:14.426
The journey through the tube
is complete, but our last pair

00:03:14.426 --> 00:03:16.236
of words needs careful handling

00:03:16.374 --> 00:03:18.224
Is removing feces excretion?

00:03:19.086 --> 00:03:21.690
It leaves the body, so surely yes?

00:03:22.407 --> 00:03:24.217
This is a classic exam trap.

00:03:24.607 --> 00:03:28.033
Egestion is removing undigested
material from the gut.

00:03:28.464 --> 00:03:32.573
Excretion is removing metabolic
waste, substances produced by

00:03:32.573 --> 00:03:34.218
the body's chemical reactions.

00:03:35.036 --> 00:03:38.280
Carbon dioxide from respiration
is excreted through the lungs.

00:03:38.590 --> 00:03:42.021
Urea is made in the liver and
removed by the kidneys in urine.

00:03:42.824 --> 00:03:43.367
Correct.

00:03:43.730 --> 00:03:47.021
Feces contain undigested
material and other contents

00:03:47.030 --> 00:03:49.228
such as bacteria and shed cells.

00:03:49.554 --> 00:03:53.675
Do not say every part is untouched
food, but passing feces is

00:03:53.675 --> 00:03:57.723
described as egestion, not the
same process as excreting urea.

00:03:58.471 --> 00:04:00.366
Different origin, different word.

00:04:00.874 --> 00:04:04.385
My imaginary exam marks are
staying inside the answer box.

00:04:05.066 --> 00:04:05.930
Let's earn them.

00:04:06.418 --> 00:04:10.204
Which test identifies starch,
and what is its positive result?

00:04:10.953 --> 00:04:14.182
Iodine solution changes from
orange-brown to blue-black.

00:04:14.698 --> 00:04:18.562
Benedict's tests reducing sugar
and needs heating in a water bath.

00:04:19.298 --> 00:04:21.725
Why does chewing help enzymes?

00:04:22.620 --> 00:04:27.991
It increases the exposed surface area of
food pieces so enzymes can act faster.

00:04:28.521 --> 00:04:33.003
Chewing itself is mechanical digestion,
not molecular chemical digestion.

00:04:33.802 --> 00:04:38.521
Complete this: bile breaks fat
molecules into fatty acids and glycerol.

00:04:39.311 --> 00:04:40.000
That sentence needs rescuing.
